---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "support@lifevisorapp.com";
const LEGAL_ENTITY = "Devsign";
const APP_NAME = "Life Visor";
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "2026-08-11";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Life Visor"
  description="The terms and conditions that govern your use of Life Visor, including subscriptions, Luna's wellness disclaimer, and your rights."
>
  <Navbar />

  <article class="w-full px-5 sm:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <span class="block w-5 h-[2px] bg-muted-2"></span>
        <span class="eyebrow text-ink-soft">TERMS OF SERVICE</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink leading-[1.1] tracking-tight mb-4">
        The <span class="highlight-yellow">rules</span> of using Life Visor
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-2 mb-12">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

      <div class="prose-content space-y-6 text-base text-muted leading-relaxed">

        <p>
          These Terms of Service (“Terms”) are a contract between you and {LEGAL_ENTITY} (“we,”
          “our,” or “us”), the company that owns and operates the {APP_NAME} mobile application,
          available on the Apple App Store and Google Play, its Luna wellness assistant, and the
          website
          <a href="https://www.lifevisorapp.com" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">lifevisorapp.com</a>
          (together, the “Service”). By downloading, installing, accessing, or using the Service,
          you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Privacy Policy</a>
          explains how we handle your information and is incorporated into these Terms by
          reference.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">1. The Service and Acceptance</h2>
        <p>
          {APP_NAME} is a wellness and self-understanding app. It includes Luna, an in-app
          assistant that reviews the information you provide and generates analysis, summaries,
          and suggestions to help you reflect on your habits and wellbeing.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must be at least 13 years old to use the Service. If you are under the age of
          majority in your jurisdiction, you may only use the Service with the involvement and
          consent of a parent or legal guardian. By using the Service, you represent that you meet
          these requirements and that any information you provide is accurate.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">2. Subscriptions and Purchases</h2>

        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink pt-4">2.1 Plans</h3>
        <p>
          Some features of the Service require a paid subscription (“Pro” or similar plans). The
          plans available, their duration, and their price are shown in the app and in the Apple
          App Store or Google Play listing at the time of purchase. Prices may vary by region and
          are subject to change; if we change the price of a plan you are subscribed to, we will
          notify you in advance as required by Apple or Google, and the new price will apply from
          your next renewal unless you cancel beforehand.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink pt-4">2.2 Free trial and automatic renewal</h3>
        <p>
          Where offered, a subscription may start with a <span class="font-semibold text-ink">7-day free trial</span>.
          If you do not cancel before the trial ends, your subscription
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink">automatically converts into a paid subscription</span>
          and payment will be charged to your Apple ID or Google Play account at confirmation of
          purchase.
        </p>
        <p>
          After that, your subscription <span class="font-semibold text-ink">automatically renews</span>
          for the same duration and at the then-current price, at the end of every billing period,
          unless you turn off auto-renewal at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.
          Your account will be charged for renewal within 24 hours prior to the end of the current
          period. Any unused portion of a free trial is forfeited once you purchase a subscription,
          where applicable.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink pt-4">2.3 How to cancel</h3>
        <p>
          Subscriptions are managed through the store you subscribed with, not through us directly.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">iOS:</span> Settings → your name → Subscriptions → {APP_NAME}.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Android:</span> Google Play app → Menu → Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions → {APP_NAME}.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can cancel at any time; access continues until the end of the period already paid
          for, and you will not be charged again after cancellation takes effect.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink pt-4">2.4 Payments and refunds</h3>
        <p>
          All payments are processed exclusively by <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Apple</span>
          (App Store) or <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Google</span> (Google Play). We do
          not process payments or store your payment details ourselves. Billing, invoicing, and
          refund requests are handled entirely by Apple or Google according to their own terms and
          policies:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT204084" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Apple's refund policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Google Play's refund policy</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not have the ability to issue refunds directly and cannot override the store's
          decision on a refund request.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink pt-4">2.5 Lifetime purchases</h3>
        <p>
          If you previously bought a one-time “lifetime” license to {APP_NAME}, that purchase
          remains valid for as long as the Service exists — it is not affected by the introduction
          of subscription plans, you will not be charged again for the features included in your
          original purchase, and these Terms apply to your continued use of the Service.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">3. Luna and Wellness Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Luna's analysis, insights, and suggestions are generated from the information you
          provide and are offered for
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink">informational and self-reflection purposes only</span>.
          They do not constitute, and must not be relied upon as, medical, psychological,
          psychiatric, therapeutic, financial, or other professional advice, diagnosis, or
          treatment.
        </p>
        <p>
          {APP_NAME} and Luna are not a substitute for consultation with a qualified physician,
          mental health professional, or other licensed provider. If you are experiencing a
          medical or mental health emergency, or are in crisis, contact your local emergency
          services or a crisis hotline immediately — do not rely on the Service. Always seek the
          advice of a qualified professional with any questions you may have regarding a medical
          or psychological condition, and never disregard or delay professional advice because of
          something Luna has generated.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">4. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          The Service — including the {APP_NAME} app, its design, the Luna assistant and its
          underlying technology, the {APP_NAME} name and logo, and all related content, software,
          and trademarks — is owned by {LEGAL_ENTITY} and is protected by intellectual property
          laws. We grant you a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
          license to use the Service for your own personal, non-commercial use, subject to these
          Terms. You may not copy, modify, distribute, sell, reverse engineer, or create derivative
          works from the Service, except as permitted by applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">5. Your Data</h2>
        <p>
          You own the data you create and enter in the Service. We process it only as described in
          our <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Privacy Policy</a>,
          and solely to operate and improve the Service and to generate Luna's analysis for you.
          Using the Service does not transfer ownership of your data to us.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">6. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose or in violation of these Terms.</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Service, other accounts, or our systems.</li>
          <li>Interfere with, disrupt, or overload the Service's infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or extract the source code or models behind the Service, except as permitted by law.</li>
          <li>Use the Service to harass, abuse, or harm another person, or to input content that is illegal, defamatory, or infringes on others' rights.</li>
          <li>Circumvent, disable, or bypass subscription or payment mechanisms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may suspend or restrict access to features if we reasonably believe your use violates
          this section.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">7. No Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The Service, including Luna's output, is provided
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink">“as is” and “as available,”</span> without
          warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including implied
          warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, or
          that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, accurate, or complete. We do not
          warrant that Luna's analysis will be accurate, complete, or suitable for your particular
          situation.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {LEGAL_ENTITY} and its officers,
          employees, and affiliates will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data, use, goodwill, or profits,
          arising out of or related to your use of, or inability to use, the Service — including
          any decision made or action taken in reliance on Luna's analysis or suggestions. Our
          total aggregate liability for any claim arising out of these Terms or the Service will
          not exceed the amount you paid us, if any, in the 12 months preceding the claim. Nothing
          in these Terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable Colombian law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">9. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using the Service and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or
          terminate your access to the Service, in whole or in part, if you breach these Terms, if
          required by law, or if we discontinue the Service, with notice where reasonably
          practicable. Sections that by their nature should survive termination (including
          Intellectual Property, No Warranties, Limitation of Liability, and Governing Law) will
          survive.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">10. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Colombia, without regard to its
          conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the
          Service will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of
          Colombia, except where applicable consumer-protection law in your country of residence
          grants you the right to bring a claim in your local courts, in which case that right is
          not affected by this clause.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time to reflect changes to the Service or for
          legal reasons. If we make material changes, we will update the effective date above and,
          where appropriate, provide notice in the app. Continuing to use the Service after changes
          take effect means you accept the updated Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink pt-8">12. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these Terms, contact us at
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
